<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Zakkur</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 800 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century-bce">9th century BCE</a> · Also known as Zakir</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Zakkur was an Aramaean king of Hamath and Lu'ash around 800 BCE, probably a usurper. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aramaic">Aramaic</a> stele, found at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tell-afis">Tell Afis</a>, ancient Hatarikka, records how the god <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baalshamin">Baalshamin</a> saved him when a coalition of kings led by Bar-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hadad">Hadad</a> of Aram-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/damascus">Damascus</a> besieged him there. It is one of the most important Old Aramaic inscriptions.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/zakkur.jpg" alt="Zakkur" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rama · CC BY-SA 2.0 fr · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zakkur_Stele_0154.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
